SEQUENCE:2026091401
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20261210T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20261210T205000
SUMMARY:Nutcracker: Cast B Dress Rehearsal – ACT II Cast B (Mandatory 
 – Production Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:*** THIS DAY ***\nCALL TIME 7:30 PM — be checked in and bac
 kstage by then. ARRIVE BY 7:15 PM.\nOn stage: 8:10 PM–8:50 PM.\nACT II
  Dress Run\; In Performance Costumes\, Hair and Makeup.\nMANDATORY — p
 roduction week.\n\n*** STANDING RULES ***\nBA: Call Time is the time dan
 cers should be check-in and backstage - Arrive 15 minutes before Call Ti
 me.\nBA: Mandatory Rehearsals (1st Rehearsal\, Rehearsals after Thanksgi
 ving and Production Week Rehearsals and Performances).\nAll Casts are ca
 lled unless a cast is named.\nSUBJECT TO CHANGE — the BA master schedu
 le\, the weekly BA emails and the BA portal are the official source. Mas
 ter: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-
 N7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\n*** COSTUME / HAIR / MAKEUP — Cherubs ***\nAngels
  - Cherubs — Costume (you provide): Pink Seamless Tights\, Flesh-tone 
 camisole leotard\; Shoes: Pink Ballet Shoes\; Makeup: Light Stage Makeup
 \; Hair: High Bun\, No Part\; Accessories (BA provides): Gold Halo headp
 iece\; Prop (BA provides): Harp\nLight Stage Makeup Instruction Sheet:\n
 • Powder matching skintone\n• Light brown eye shadow applied to the 
 crease with an eye shadow brush\n• Dark Brown/Black eyeliner and black
  mascara. No fake lashes.\n• Blush on the cheeks (be sure to apply ple
 nty so dancer doesn’t look washed out in the stage lights)\n• Red or
  Dark Red lipstick\nDancers of Color may wear flesh tone tights and fles
 h tone ballet shoes.\nCostume Care Guidelines:\n• Handle costume piece
 s with care while changing to prevent damage to delicate fabrics\n• Pr
 omptly notify Ballet Arkansas in the event of costume damage at the poin
 t of discovery\, no matter how significant\n• Never throw costumes or 
 accessories on the floor\, or hang costumes by their elastic straps\n•
  Refrain from sitting on the floor while in costume\n• Do not attempt 
 to alter\, mend\, clean\, or launder any costume or accessory\n• Never
  apply stage make-up while in costume and shall take great care to refra
 in from smudging make-up on costume during its removal\n• Refrain from
  the use of spray perfume or cologne while in costume\n• Never wear an
 y garment not assigned to cast member\n• Do not handle or consume food
  or beverage while in costume\, with the exception of water\n• Do not 
 remove costumes from their assigned dressing rooms or from the theater\n
 • Remove all bobby pins used to secure head pieces and wigs following 
 their use\n• Return all headpieces to their assigned bags\n• Comply 
 fully with any and all updates to Ballet Arkansas’ wardrobe policies\n
 • Do not pack markers\, paints\, colored drinks or anything that may d
 amage or stain costumes.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT1H
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Nutcracker in 1 hour
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
